     "\r<br>On Mon, May 9, 2016 at 1:27 PM, John Rauser &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jra...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; &quot;The error seems clear to me.&quot;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I too suffer from R Stockholm Syndrome, &quot;in which hostages express empathy\r<br>&gt; and sympathy and have positive feelings toward their captors, sometimes to\r<br>&gt; the point of defending and identifying with the captors. These feelings are\r<br>&gt; generally considered irrational in light of the danger or risk endured by\r<br>&gt; the victims, who essentially mistake a lack of abuse from their captors for\r<br>&gt; an act of kindness.&quot;  (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockholm_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockholm_syndrome&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366740473000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MhzJyDQqybfDy0bY3niWG\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockholm_syndrome</a>)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Your advice is spot on, and I&#39;m sure appreciated by the OP, but we too\r<br>&gt; easily forget how cryptic R&#39;s error messages are for new users.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I mean no disrespect or offense... your opening sentence just made me\r<br>&gt; chuckle, and then made me think.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Best,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; -J\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Sat, May 7, 2016 at 5:44 AM, Ista Zahn &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ista...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; The error seems clear to me. There is no column named &#39;visit&#39; in data. Use\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; names(data)\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; and\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; str(data)\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; to see what&#39;s in there, and remember that R (unlike SAS) is case\r<br>&gt;&gt; sensitive.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Best,\r<br>&gt;&gt; Ista\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; On May 7, 2016 8:19 AM, &quot;SRINI&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">somka...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; I am importing SAS dataset  to R and using as source data to draw a graph\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; in ggplot2. It produces only values with list not graph. Error is given\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; below. can you please help me troubleshooting?. Thanks.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; library(ggplot2)\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; library(haven)\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; data = read_sas(&#39;C:\\\\Users\\\\kk\\\\Documents\\\\adpc1.sas7bdat&#39;)\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; adpcc = ggplot(data, aes(x=visit, y=pcstresn)) + geom_point()\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; adpcc\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Error in eval(expr, envir, enclos) : object &#39;visit&#39; not found\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; --\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; --\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; mailing list.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Please provide a reproducible example:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366740473000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33PMD-ET8iOH4Mfj_59s0Q\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a>\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366740