     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi All,</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; .libPaths()</div><div><br></div><div>[1] &quot;C:/Users/kks/AppData/Local/Temp/RtmpKWQd5u/downloaded_packages&quot;</div><div>[2] &quot;C:/Program Files/R/R-3.4.2/library&quot;</div></div><div><br></div><div>Installed ggplot2 package in library 1. above after upgrading to latest R version. . But when i load, it throws following error.</div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">Error in library(ggplot2) : there is no package called ‘ggplot2’</font></div><div><br></div><div>Any help will be appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Kamal.</div><div><br></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
